(1) On-call rules (firm)

The clinic requires continuous overnight and weekend emergency coverage every day of the year with no gaps. Coverage is assigned by strict rotation so that each physician carries an equal share of call across the scheduling period. The medical director’s mandate is explicit: "Overnight and weekend emergency call must be covered every single day of the year with no gaps; each physician is assigned an equal share by strict rotation. No swaps for religious reasons, period — even if a willing colleague has already offered to cover the shift, a religious request is not grounds to move it." Accordingly: religious requests do not justify reassignment or swaps and will be denied. Non-religious swap requests may be considered only with written approval from the medical director and only if the swap preserves exact equality of total assigned call days for the affected quarter. Unauthorized or informal swaps are prohibited and subject to corrective action.

